        <article class="prose">
            <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
            <p>SupportFlow is a customer support platform built and operated by Tatah Withney. It lets organizations receive, assign and resolve support requests. This policy explains what personal information SupportFlow handles and why.</p>

            <h2 id="collect">Information we collect</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your name, email address, role and the organization you belong to.</li>
                <li><strong>Password:</strong> stored only as a one-way hash. We cannot read your password.</li>
                <li><strong>Support content:</strong> the requests you create, their category and priority, and the messages exchanged in each conversation.</li>
                <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> basic server logs such as request times and IP addresses, created by our hosting provider to keep the service running.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 id="use">How we use it</h2>
            <p>We use your information to create and secure your account, show you the right requests, let agents and managers respond, and keep the service reliable. We do not use your information for advertising and we do not sell it.</p>

            <h2 id="orgs">Organizations and access</h2>
            <p>SupportFlow is multi-tenant: each organization has its own workspace. Customers can see only their own requests. Agents can see requests assigned to them. Managers and administrators of an organization can see the users and requests in that organization. Data in one organization is not shown to another.</p>

            <h2 id="share">Sharing</h2>
            <p>We share information only with the service providers needed to run SupportFlow, namely our application host and our database provider, and when the law requires it. These providers process data on our behalf.</p>

            <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
            <p>Passwords are hashed, sign-in tokens expire, and access is limited by role and organization. No online service is completely secure, so please use a strong, unique password and sign out on shared devices.</p>

            <h2 id="storage">Browser storage</h2>
            <p>SupportFlow stores a sign-in token and your chosen portal in your browser's local storage so you stay signed in. It also remembers that you dismissed the storage notice. We do not use advertising or tracking cookies. Signing out removes the token.</p>

            <h2 id="retention">Retention</h2>
            <p>We keep your information while your account is active or while your organization needs it to provide support. You can ask for your information to be corrected or deleted at any time.</p>

            <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
            <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct or delete your personal data, and to object to or restrict certain processing. To exercise these rights, contact us using the details below.</p>

            <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
            <p>SupportFlow is not intended for children, and we do not knowingly collect their personal information.</p>

            <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
            <p>We may update this policy as the service changes. The date below shows when it was last revised.</p>
            <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 24 October 2026</p>

            <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
